    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "A series of 100 laparoscopic sterilizations, performed on an outpatient basis, is reported. 66 patients experienced abdominal pain, 52 experienced shoulder tip pain, 21 became nauseous, and 10 vomited. 2 patients required emergency hospitalization. The procedure was well tolerated by most patients. No pregnancies have been reported to date."
    }
